# postui-top — caps.decl
#
# Wave: postui v1 reference apps
# Milestone: M1 (scaffold + sys_taskinfo poll loop)
# Doc:  paideia-os/postui/docs/design.md §3.1 (widget mix + data
#       source for /bin/top); paideia-os/postui/design/architecture.md
#       §5.1 (error-band allocation table).
#
# postui-top is the top(1)-style task viewer that consumes the postui
# widget library at exec time. Its cap footprint at M1-001 covers
# every substrate the poll + eventual render paths will touch — the
# scaffold declares the full set up front so the M2 render-landing and
# M4 semantic-pipe-emit landings do not need to reopen the manifest
# for a re-sign.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_TUI_CANVAS — the render substrate (postui/docs/design.md §2.1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# postui-top holds one canvas cap per rendering surface (single canvas
# for the fullscreen top view at M2; the M3 tabs view stays inside
# one canvas via sub-region draws rather than a compositor split).
#
# Rights layout (mirrors R_TTY_* discipline; see postui/docs/design.md
# §2.1 "Rights" table):
#
#   R_TUI_PRESENT   0x002   diff + emit a frame (the write analogue)
#   R_TUI_INVOKE    0x008   query ops (rows, cols, id, tty_id)
#   R_TUI_RESIZE    0x010   TUI_OP_RESIZE / TUI_OP_CLEAR
#   R_TUI_REVOKE    0x020   teardown the row
#   R_TUI_MINT      0x200   derive a canvas from a KIND_MEMORY parent
#   R_TUI_OBSERVE   0x400   debug printer
#
# At M1-001 postui-top's poll module (src/poll.pdx) does NOT touch the
# canvas — the sys_taskinfo poll runs before any render. The mint and
# present rights are declared HERE so the M1-005 render landing (which
# introduces terminal_init + frame_render + frame_present through
# postui) does not need a caps.decl churn:
#
#   * mint    — postui-top mints its top-level canvas at Main::main
#               startup via sys_cap_derive against a KIND_MEMORY parent
#               (M1-005 landing).
#   * present — every frame_render tail invokes TUI_OP_PRESENT via
#               postui's tcc_present wrapper (M2-onwards render path).
#
# R_TUI_INVOKE / R_TUI_RESIZE / R_TUI_REVOKE are DEFERRED (declared at
# M1-005 when the render path first exercises them); adding them at
# this landing would over-declare authority the M1-001 poll surface
# never uses.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_TTY — the input + physical-sink substrate (postui/docs/design.md
# §2.5)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two independent uses (mirror postui's own caps.decl):
#
#   * write — the canvas is provably wired to a live KIND_TTY at mint
#     time (postui/docs/design.md §2.1: the row's tty_slot is validated
#     via tty_tail_valid at cap_handler_tui_canvas mint). TUI_OP_PRESENT
#     emits its ANSI byte stream through the tty_slot; the write right
#     is transitively required at postui-top mint time even though
#     postui-top code never issues TTY_OP_WRITE itself.
#
#   * read — the primary input path once postui.M4-007 lands (Terminal::
#     terminal_read_input probes KIND_TTY raw-mode). The M1-001 poll
#     surface never reads input; declared here so the M3 tabs-toggle
#     landing does not need to widen the manifest.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_MEMORY — the canvas backing store (postui/docs/design.md §2.1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# KIND_TUI_CANVAS derives over KIND_MEMORY (= KIND_PAGE, 4). postui-top
# mints a KIND_MEMORY region sized 2 * rows * cols * CELL_BYTES at
# M1-005 startup and hands it to sys_cap_derive(KIND_TUI_CANVAS, ...);
# the derived canvas cap is what postui subsequently invokes for every
# PRESENT. The KIND_MEMORY authority is not held beyond the derive.
#
requires:
- KIND_TUI_CANVAS(mint, present)
- KIND_TTY(write, read)
- KIND_MEMORY(mint, revoke)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Syscall dependencies (informational; not consumed by the InitCap
# sidecar — the syscall gate is a kernel-side dispatch decision, not a
# per-process cap check at M1). Enumerated here so downstream tooling
# (release lint, dependency-audit) that walks the tree can trace
# postui-top's SC+ surface without reading every .pdx source.
#
# The M1-001 poll path uses exactly two syscalls beyond what postui's
# own render path already declares:
#
#   * sysno 66 — sys_clock_read_ns() -> u64 ns
#                Monotonic ns-since-boot counter. PollLoop uses it to
#                gate the fixed-interval poll_tick refresh (converting
#                the interval_ticks arg to a compatible ns-domain
#                deadline via shift, per src/poll.pdx §Tick semantics).
#   * sysno 83 — sys_taskinfo(idx, user_buf_va) -> 0|-ENOENT|-ESRCH|-EFAULT
#                Ring-3 task-table introspection (design/user/syscall-
#                table.md row 83, paideia-os). Fills a 64-byte record
#                per live task; poll_tick iterates idx = 0..row_cap and
#                transcodes into the postui-top 48-byte task_row form.
#   * sysno 115 — sys_semantic_send(schema_hash, rec_ptr, rec_len)
#                              -> 0|-EAGAIN|-EINVAL|-EFAULT
#                Enqueues one typed record into the global semantic-
#                pipe ring (4KB, 16 slots x 256B). ABI documented in
#                the postui-top#6 issue and programmed against in
#                src/semantic_emit.pdx (M4-001 landing). The kernel
#                dispatch body is NOT YET LIVE at paideia-os HEAD --
#                every invocation returns -ENOSYS
#                (0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFDA) until postui-top#7 / M4-002
#                lands src/kernel/core/syscall/handlers/
#                sys_semantic_send.pdx and the sysno-115 dispatch
#                wiring in src/kernel/core/syscall/dispatch.pdx.
#                Enumerated here so downstream dependency-audit sees
#                the transport for the declared TaskRow@0.1 output
#                schema below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
syscalls:
- sys_clock_read_ns @ 66
- sys_taskinfo      @ 83
- sys_semantic_send @ 115

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Declared output schemas
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# postui-top emits one first-class semantic-pipe schema at M4-004:
#
#   * TaskRow@0.1 — one record per live task, mirroring the internal
#                   task_row struct (pid u64, state u64, ticks_cpu u64,
#                   mem_kb u64, name_ptr u64, name_len u64 = 48B).
#                   Emitted through the KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT postui-top
#                   binds at Main::main startup (M2-005 wire-in). Every
#                   downstream scraper (e.g. a monitoring daemon that
#                   pulls TaskRow via `top | scraper`) reads the same
#                   32-byte-BLAKE3 schema hash under the libpdx-
#                   semantic-pipe v1 contract.
#
# At M1-001 the emitter path is scaffolding only (poll.pdx populates
# the in-memory row set; no envelope encoder runs). The schema name
# is declared here so the M4-004 landing does not need to introduce
# it and the downstream dependency-audit tree already sees postui-top
# as a TaskRow producer.
declares_output_schemas:
- TaskRow@0.1
